## Context
Child of tracker 0974. Phase 0 of `docs/portable-model-capability-policy.md`:
define the semantic controls and a Claude adapter mapping that reproduces
today's concrete choices exactly. No live model or effort selection changes.

Today's choices to reproduce (verified on main 2026-09-24): `/hunt` coding
executor `opus`; `/raid` orchestrator `claude-sonnet-5` in frontmatter,
reviewers `sonnet`, mechanical checks `haiku`, coders `opus`; `team-lead` has
no pin and inherits the session. The inheritance is recorded as today's
behaviour, not endorsed — Phase 2 changes it.

## Exit criteria
- [x] A vocabulary module or config names the two controls and their values
- [x] A Claude mapping resolves each level to a concrete enum token; `auto`
      maps to a configured tier, never to session inheritance (doc invariant 9)
- [x] A test enumerates current launch sites and shows each resolves to its
      existing model/effort, and fails if one would change (positive control:
      alter one mapping entry and watch it go red)
- [x] No skill, agent or rule file changes behaviour in this PR
- [ ] `make check` passes
